  "summary": "The Leaning Tower of Pisa is the bell tower of the cathedral on Piazza del Duomo in Pisa, Italy. Building began in August 1173 and continued for roughly two centuries with two long interruptions. The Opera della Primaziale Pisana gives its height as 58.36 m and its external diameter as 15 m.",
